Update all encoding option values according to the new naming conventions and handle the return type change:

```diff
- await execa('node', ['file.js'], {encoding: null});
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {encoding: 'buffer'});

- await execa('node', ['file.js'], {encoding: 'utf-8'});
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {encoding: 'utf8'});

- await execa('node', ['file.js'], {encoding: 'UTF8'});
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {encoding: 'utf8'});

- await execa('node', ['file.js'], {encoding: 'utf-16le'});
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {encoding: 'utf16le'});

- await execa('node', ['file.js'], {encoding: 'ucs2'});
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {encoding: 'utf16le'});

- await execa('node', ['file.js'], {encoding: 'ucs-2'});
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {encoding: 'utf16le'});

- await execa('node', ['file.js'], {encoding: 'binary'});
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {encoding: 'latin1'});
```

Note that when using `encoding: 'buffer'`, the result is now a `Uint8Array` instead of a `Buffer`. If you need a `Buffer` specifically, you can convert it:

```javascript
const result = await execa('node', ['file.js'], {encoding: 'buffer'});
const buffer = Buffer.from(result.stdout);
```

Replace the pipe*() methods with appropriate options:

```diff
- await execa('node', ['file.js']).pipeStdout('output.txt');
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {stdout: {file: 'output.txt'}});

- await execa('node', ['file.js']).pipeStderr('output.txt');
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {stderr: {file: 'output.txt'}});

- await execa('node', ['file.js']).pipeAll('output.txt');
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {
+   stdout: {file: 'output.txt'},
+   stderr: {file: 'output.txt'},
+ });
```

Replace stream piping with appropriate options:

```diff
- await execa('node', ['file.js']).pipeStdout(stream);
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {stdout: ['pipe', stream]});

- await execa('node', ['file.js']).pipeStderr(stream);
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {stderr: ['pipe', stream]});

- await execa('node', ['file.js']).pipeAll(stream);
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {
+   stdout: ['pipe', stream],
+   stderr: ['pipe', stream],
+ });
```

Replace the old pipe methods with the new subprocess.pipe() method:

```diff
- await execa('node', ['file.js']).pipeStdout(execa('node', ['other.js']));
+ await execa('node', ['file.js']).pipe('node', ['other.js']);

- await execa('node', ['file.js']).pipeStderr(execa('node', ['other.js']));
+ await execa('node', ['file.js']).pipe('node', ['other.js'], {from: 'stderr'});

- await execa('node', ['file.js']).pipeAll(execa('node', ['other.js']));
+ await execa('node', ['file.js']).pipe('node', ['other.js'], {from: 'all'});
```

Update all references to the signal option in execa method calls:

```diff
- await execa('node', ['file.js'], {signal: abortController.signal});
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {cancelSignal: abortController.signal});

- execaSync('node', ['file.js'], {signal: abortController.signal});
+ execaSync('node', ['file.js'], {cancelSignal: abortController.signal});
```

Update all references to error.killed to error.isTerminated:

```diff
try {
  await execa('node', ['file.js']);
} catch (error) {
-  if (error.killed) {
+  if (error.isTerminated) {
    // ...
  }
}
```

Replace subprocess.cancel() with subprocess.kill():

```diff
- subprocess.cancel();
+ subprocess.kill();
```

Or use the cancelSignal option with an AbortController:

```js
const abortController = new AbortController();
const subprocess = execa('node', ['file.js'], {cancelSignal: abortController.signal});
// Later when you want to cancel:
abortController.abort();
```

Move the option from subprocess.kill() to the execa() options and rename it:

```diff
- const subprocess = execa('node', ['file.js']);
- subprocess.kill('SIGTERM', {forceKillAfterTimeout: 1000});
+ const subprocess = execa('node', ['file.js'], {forceKillAfterDelay: 1000});
+ subprocess.kill('SIGTERM');
```

Update the verbose option to use the new string enum values:

```diff
- await execa('node', ['file.js'], {verbose: false});
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {verbose: 'none'});

- await execa('node', ['file.js'], {verbose: true});
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {verbose: 'short'});
```

Rename the execPath option to nodePath and add the node: true option if you need it to have an effect:

```diff
- await execa('node', ['file.js'], {execPath: './path/to/node'});
+ await execa('node', ['file.js'], {nodePath: './path/to/node', node: true});
```

Remove functions and symbols from objects passed to subprocess.send() or explicitly set the serialization option to 'json':

```diff
- subprocess.send({example: true, getExample() {}});
+ subprocess.send({example: true});
```

Or set the serialization option to 'json':

```js
const subprocess = execa('node', ['file.js'], {serialization: 'json'});
subprocess.send({example: true, getExample() {}}); // Functions will be removed silently
```

Ensure pipe() is called immediately after creating the subprocess, with no delays:

```diff
const subprocess = execa('node', ['file.js']);
- setTimeout(() => {
  subprocess.stdout.pipe(process.stdout);
- }, 0);
```

Update all signal names to use uppercase format for both the killSignal option and subprocess.kill() method:

```diff
- const subprocess = execa('node', ['file.js'], {killSignal: 'sigterm'});
+ const subprocess = execa('node', ['file.js'], {killSignal: 'SIGTERM'});

- subprocess.kill('sigterm');
+ subprocess.kill('SIGTERM');
```
